{"seq":60,"slug":"database-sharding-partitioning","title":"数据库分片与分区","stage":"DONE","category":"cs-fundamentals","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/database-sharding-partitioning","rating":{"composite":3.84,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.6,"coverage":3.5,"positioning":4,"strategic":4.33},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introMarkdown":"# 数据库分片与分区\n\n当一张表从几百万行长到几十亿行、当单台数据库的 CPU、内存与磁盘 I/O 同时逼近上限时，垂直加机器（scale up）的边际收益会迅速塌方，而水平拆分（scale out）成为唯一可持续的出路。分片与分区就是把这件事做对、做稳、做得能长期运维的工程学问。它不是某个数据库的一个开关，而是一组贯穿数据模型、查询路径、事务边界与运维体系的设计决策——一旦选错分区键或低估了跨分片查询的代价，代价往往要到数据已经分布在上百个节点之后才暴露出来，而那时迁移成本极高。\n\n这个 hub 按四条主线层层递进。第一章「基础」打地基：先讲清楚为什么单机会成为瓶颈、扩展有哪些维度，再辨析「分区」与「分片」这两个常被混用却本质不同的概念，最后落到一切设计的起点——分区键的选择。地基稳了，第二章「分片策略」回答核心问题：数据具体怎么分到各个分片去？范围分片、哈希分片、目录分片与一致性哈希各有其适用场景与代价，理解它们的取舍是后续一切的前提。\n\n第三章「挑战」直面分片之后必然遇到的三道难题：跨分片的查询与聚合为什么变慢变复杂、热点与数据倾斜如何让「均分」沦为空谈、以及当容量再次告急时如何在不停机的前提下再平衡与重分片。这些难题不是策略选错的结果，而是分布式数据的固有张力，必须正面应对。第四章「运维」则把视角拉到长期：分片路由与中间件如何对应用屏蔽分布细节、全局二级索引如何在分片之上支撑非分区键查询、以及监控与容量规划如何让你在崩溃之前就看见趋势。\n\n四章之间是严格的依赖关系：没有基础就谈不上策略，没有策略就无所谓挑战，而运维是让前三者在生产环境里长久成立的保障。读完这个 hub，你应当能够独立判断一个系统该不该分片、该怎么分、分了之后会撞上哪些墙、以及如何把它平稳地运营下去。建议按章顺序阅读；各篇之间已用交叉链接织成网络，遇到前置概念可顺链回溯。\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"基础","docCount":3,"url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/database-sharding-partitioning/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"why-partition","title":"为何分区：单机瓶颈与扩展维度","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/database-sharding-partitioning/foundations/why-partition"},{"seq":2,"slug":"partitioning-vs-sharding","title":"分区与分片：概念辨析","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/database-sharding-partitioning/foundations/partitioning-vs-sharding"},{"seq":3,"slug":"partition-keys","title":"分区键的选择","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/database-sharding-partitioning/foundations/partition-keys"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"strategies","title":"分片策略","docCount":3,"url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/database-sharding-partitioning/strategies","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"range-partitioning","title":"范围分片","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/database-sharding-partitioning/strategies/range-partitioning"},{"seq":2,"slug":"hash-partitioning","title":"哈希分片","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/database-sharding-partitioning/strategies/hash-partitioning"},{"seq":3,"slug":"directory-consistent-hashing","title":"目录分片与一致性哈希","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/database-sharding-partitioning/strategies/directory-consistent-hashing"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"challenges","title":"挑战","docCount":3,"url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/database-sharding-partitioning/challenges","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"cross-shard-queries","title":"跨分片查询与聚合","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/database-sharding-partitioning/challenges/cross-shard-queries"},{"seq":2,"slug":"hotspots-skew","title":"热点与数据倾斜","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/database-sharding-partitioning/challenges/hotspots-skew"},{"seq":3,"slug":"rebalancing-resharding","title":"再平衡与重分片","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/database-sharding-partitioning/challenges/rebalancing-resharding"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"operations","title":"运维","docCount":3,"url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/database-sharding-partitioning/operations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"shard-routing","title":"分片路由与中间件","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/database-sharding-partitioning/operations/shard-routing"},{"seq":2,"slug":"global-secondary-indexes","title":"全局二级索引","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/database-sharding-partitioning/operations/global-secondary-indexes"},{"seq":3,"slug":"monitoring-capacity","title":"监控与容量规划","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/database-sharding-partitioning/operations/monitoring-capacity"}]}]}